Task 1: Prepare for System Registration
Subtask 1.1: Verify Network Connectivity
First, ensure your client systems can communicate with the Satellite server.

Check DNS resolution for the Satellite server:
nslookup satellite.example.com
Test network connectivity to the Satellite server:
ping -c 4 satellite.example.com
Verify Satellite services are accessible:
curl -k https://satellite.example.com/pub/
Subtask 1.2: Install Required Packages
Ensure the subscription-manager package is installed and up-to-date.

Check if subscription-manager is installed:
rpm -qa | grep subscription-manager
Install or update subscription-manager if needed:
sudo yum install -y subscription-manager
Verify the installation:
subscription-manager --version
Subtask 1.3: Download Satellite CA Certificate
The client system needs the Satellite server's CA certificate for secure communication.

Download the CA certificate from Satellite:
sudo wget -O /etc/rhsm/ca/katello-server-ca.pem \
  https://satellite.example.com/pub/katello-server-ca.pem
Verify the certificate was downloaded successfully:
sudo ls -la /etc/rhsm/ca/katello-server-ca.pem
Check certificate details:
sudo openssl x509 -in /etc/rhsm/ca/katello-server-ca.pem -text -noout | head -20
Task 2: Register Hosts Using Subscription Manager
Subtask 2.1: Basic Registration Process
Register your RHEL system to the Satellite server using subscription-manager.

Clean any existing registration (if applicable):
sudo subscription-manager clean
Register the system to Satellite:
sudo subscription-manager register \
  --serverurl=https://satellite.example.com:443/rhsm \
  --baseurl=https://satellite.example.com/pulp/repos \
  --org="Default_Organization" \
  --username=admin \
  --password=redhat123
Verify registration status:
sudo subscription-manager status
List available subscriptions:
sudo subscription-manager list --available
Subtask 2.2: Attach Subscriptions
After registration, attach appropriate subscriptions to enable repositories.

Auto-attach subscriptions based on system hardware:
sudo subscription-manager attach --auto
Verify attached subscriptions:
sudo subscription-manager list --consumed
Check enabled repositories:
sudo subscription-manager repos --list-enabled
Subtask 2.3: Enable Required Repositories
Enable specific repositories needed for your RHEL system.

List all available repositories:
sudo subscription-manager repos --list
Enable BaseOS and AppStream repositories:
sudo subscription-manager repos \
  --enable=rhel-8-for-x86_64-baseos-rpms \
  --enable=rhel-8-for-x86_64-appstream-rpms
Verify repository configuration:
sudo yum repolist enabled
Task 3: Apply Activation Keys for RHEL Systems
Subtask 3.1: Create Activation Key on Satellite
First, create an activation key through the Satellite web interface or API.

Access Satellite web interface at https://satellite.example.com

Navigate to Content > Activation Keys

Create new activation key with these settings:

Name: RHEL8-Production
Environment: Production
Content View: RHEL8-CV
Usage Limit: Unlimited
Add subscriptions to the activation key:

Select appropriate RHEL subscriptions
Configure auto-attach settings
Subtask 3.2: Register Using Activation Key
Use the activation key for automated registration without username/password.

Unregister current system (for demonstration):
sudo subscription-manager unregister
Register using activation key:
sudo subscription-manager register \
  --serverurl=https://satellite.example.com:443/rhsm \
  --baseurl=https://satellite.example.com/pulp/repos \
  --org="Default_Organization" \
  --activationkey="RHEL8-Production"
Verify registration with activation key:
sudo subscription-manager identity
Check auto-attached subscriptions:
sudo subscription-manager list --consumed
Subtask 3.3: Configure System Using Activation Key
Activation keys can automatically configure repositories and install packages.

Verify enabled repositories from activation key:
sudo yum repolist enabled
Install katello-agent for enhanced Satellite integration:
sudo yum install -y katello-agent
Start and enable goferd service:
sudo systemctl enable --now goferd
Verify service status:
sudo systemctl status goferd
Task 4: Validate Registration via Satellite Dashboard
Subtask 4.1: Access Satellite Web Interface
Verify system registration through the Satellite dashboard.

Open web browser and navigate to:

https://satellite.example.com
Login with credentials:

Username: admin
Password: redhat123
Navigate to Hosts > All Hosts to view registered systems

Subtask 4.2: Verify Host Information
Check that your registered system appears correctly in Satellite.

